{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4769","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4769/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4769/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4769/events","html_url":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4769","id":1640521755,"node_id":"I_kwDOCA8Bec5hyGAb","number":4769,"title":"Pickling deque subclasses ignores their `__dict__`.","user":{"login":"DimitrisJim","id":8123587,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMjM1ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8123587?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim","html_url":"https://github.com/DimitrisJim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DimitrisJim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":947386063,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NDczODYwNjM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/labels/C-bug","name":"C-bug","color":"f5f1fd","default":false,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1397253490,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzk3MjUzNDkw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/labels/C-compat","name":"C-compat","color":"f5f1fd","default":false,"description":"A discrepancy between RustPython and CPython","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2023-03-25T13:37:33Z","updated_at":"2023-03-25T18:01:23Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Caught after updating `test_deque.py`. In RustPython, pickling a deque subclass ignores its `__dict__`:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n>>>>> import pickle\r\n>>>>> from collections import deque\r\n>>>>> class Deque(deque): pass\r\n>>>>> d = Deque()\r\n>>>>> d.x = \"value\"\r\n>>>>> e = pickle.loads(pickle.dumps(pickle.HIGHEST_PROTOCOL))\r\n>>>>> e.__dict__\r\n{}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhile in Python, `__dict__` is correctly returned as `{'x': 'value'}`.\r\n\r\nThis doesn't appear to be the case with some other collections like `list` and `dict` so those could probably serve as an inspiration for what might be missing in `deque`.\r\n\r\nFor testing purposes, see [`test_copy_pickle`](https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/blob/25ca331dc81e617498465ecdb2f848ec81025f71/Lib/test/test_deque.py#L818) in `Lib/test/test_deque.py`.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/4769/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}